# Release, updates & project org (Rosario Cards)

## After shipping a feature (small checklist)

When a feature is **committed/pushed** or a version is bumped:

1. **Update toast/banner** — Confirm the app can show “new version available” (PWA service worker + `appUpdateAvailable`). Banner must include a **short feature summary**, not only the version number.
2. **Release notes** — Add bullets to `src/data/releaseNotes.js` (`CURRENT` = shipped, `UPCOMING` = next). Keep it short (token budget).
3. **Easy “check later”** — Users must reach notes without hunting:
   - Top-right **Ajustes** button (label/title, **not** a classic gear — do not call it “gear” in docs/UI copy).
   - Tap the **version badge** (`vX.Y.Z`) → Novedades.
   - Settings → **Novedades** / **Estudio de imágenes**.
4. **Git** — Prefer **commit** (and push only if user asked) so work lives in the worktree/remote. Do not leave large feature work uncommitted across sessions unless user said so.

## What we have vs what we will implement

- Source of truth for **shipped this version**: `src/data/releaseNotes.js` → `CURRENT`.
- Source of truth for **next**: `UPCOMING` in the same file (manual; not auto-hooked to git worktrees yet — too expensive for tokens).
- Optional later: GitHub Projects / Wiki for roadmap; do **not** build a full in-app git worktree browser unless requested.

## GitHub features to remind the user (when relevant)

Obscure but useful for this solo/small project — mention occasionally, don’t nag every turn:

| Feature | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| **Wiki** | Long-form handbook, liturgy notes, image inventory |
| **Projects** | Kanban: shipped / next / blocked |
| **Discussions** | Design notes without polluting issues |
| **Releases** | Tag `v0.3.x` + paste `releaseNotes` bullets |
| **Milestones** | Group issues by version |
| **Codespaces / worktrees** | Parallel experiments (agent may use local worktrees) |
| **Actions** | CI build/test on push (if/when added) |

## UI access facts (do not invent icons)

- **Ajustes** = top-right circular control (sunburst/asterisk icon historically; must have `title`/`aria-label` “Ajustes”). There is **no** settings gear icon users recognize.
- **Sync** = adjacent circular control (cloud/sync).
- **Estudio de imágenes** = Ajustes → “Estudio de imágenes”, or route `/assets`.
- **Update banner** = top of shell when SW has a waiting worker; “Actualizar” applies update.

## Token budget

Only implement **small steps** for roadmap/update UX. Prefer editing `releaseNotes.js` + banner text over new subsystems.
